@[expose] public section

/-!
# The degree inequality for orders of vanishing, and finiteness as the case of equality

Proof of `Ring.finite_maximalSpectrum_and_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_eq_iff_finite`
(Stacks 02MM): for `A ⊆ B` an extension of domains with `A` local Noetherian of Krull dimension
at most one, `B` of finite type over `A` and the induced extension `L/K` of fraction fields
finite, the ring `B` is semi-local, and for every nonzero `x` in the maximal ideal of `A` the sum
over the maximal ideals `𝔪` of `B` of `[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x)` is at most
`[L : K] · ord_A(x)`, with equality exactly when `A → B` is finite.

## Implementation notes

Semi-locality is proved here in full, and along a route slightly different from the source's.
The source invokes Stacks 02MA, which bounds the fibre of `Spec B → Spec A` over a height one
prime; that accounts for the maximal ideals of `B` lying over `𝔪_A`, but not for a maximal ideal
lying over `(0)`, which occurs: for `A` a discrete valuation ring and `B = K` its fraction field
— a finite type `A`-algebra — the only maximal ideal of `B` is `(0)`. The gap is closed by
`eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot_of_isAlgebraic` below: in an algebraic extension of domains a prime
contracting to `(0)` is `(0)`, because clearing the leading zeros from an algebraic relation
`∑ aᵢ bⁱ = 0` exhibits a nonzero element of the base inside the ideal generated by `b`. So the
maximal ideals of `B` are among `(0)` together with the primes over `𝔪_A`, and there are finitely
many of the latter by Stacks 02MA — which applies because `𝔪_A` has height one as soon as `A` is
not a field, `Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A` bounding the height above and the chain `(0) ⊊ 𝔪_A` bounding
it below. When `A` is a field the numerical assertions are vacuous, since `𝔪_A = (0)` has no
nonzero element, and `B` has `(0)` for its only maximal ideal.

The numerical assertions rest on two further results of the source, both of them already proved
in this repository. Stacks 02MJ is
`finite_maximalSpectrum_and_ordInt_norm_eq_finsum_inertiaDeg_mul_ordInt` at the end of this file,
whose norm formula is `ord_norm_eq_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/OrderOfVanishing/Norm.lean`: for `A ⊆ B` a finite extension of domains,
`ord_A(Nm_{L/K}(y)) = ∑_𝔪 [κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] ord_{B_𝔪}(y)`. Stacks 00QB is
`quasiFinite_exists_finite_subalgebra` in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/ZariskisMainTheorem.lean`,
Zariski's main theorem in the form that produces a finite `R`-subalgebra `S'' ⊆ S` inside the
integral closure for which `Spec S → Spec S''` is an open embedding and `S''_g ≅ S_g` on the
basic opens inside the image; the localisations of `S''` at the contractions `S'' ∩ 𝔪` therefore
agree with those of `B` at `𝔪`. The inequality is then 02MJ applied to that `C = S''` at `y = x`,
the maximal ideals of `C` other than the contractions `C ∩ 𝔪` contributing the nonnegative
defect, and equality forces there to be no such extra maximal ideal, whence `C ⊆ B` induces a
bijection on maximal ideals and an isomorphism on the localisations there, so that for `b ∈ B` the
ideal `{c ∈ C | c b ∈ C}` of `C` lies in no maximal ideal of `C` and is therefore `C` itself.
Two mismatches of shape have to be crossed to use 02MJ here, and are crossed in
`sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite`: 02MJ is stated with `ordInt` valued in `ℤ` and with
`Ideal.inertiaDeg'` rather than `Ring.ord` valued in `ℕ∞` and `Ideal.inertiaDeg`, and it sums over
a `Fintype (MaximalSpectrum B)` rather than as a `finsum`. Both orders of vanishing occurring are
finite (`Ring.ord_ne_top` at a nonzero divisor), so the identity descends from `ℤ` to `ℕ` and
lifts back to `ℕ∞`; every maximal ideal of `B` lies over `𝔪_A` because `B` is integral over `A`,
which is what makes `Ideal.inertiaDeg'` and `Ideal.inertiaDeg` agree there. 02MJ also asks for the
localisations `B_𝔪` as `L`-algebras with `IsFractionRing` and `IsScalarTower` data; these are
supplied by `IsLocalization.localizationAlgebraOfSubmonoidLe` along
`𝔪.primeCompl ≤ nonZeroDivisors B`. The exact count for a finite extension is isolated as
`sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite`, and the inequality together with the case of equality as
`sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_finite_of_eq`; the latter two are proved in one lemma because they
share the whole construction of `C`, the equality being read off from the same subsum. That the
subsum is a strict part of the total unless the injection `𝔪 ↦ C ∩ 𝔪` is onto is the arithmetic
of `ℕ∞` in `sum_comp_le_and_surjective_of_eq`, and the two facts about a maximal ideal of `C`
that make it strict are `inertiaDeg_mul_ord_ne_zero`.

The comparison of `C` with `B` at a maximal ideal `𝔪` of `B` rests on the single property of `C`
recorded in `exists_finite_subalgebra_forall_isMaximal`: some `g ∈ C` avoids `𝔪` and every element
of `B` is carried into `C` by a power of `g`. From it, `ord_localization_comap_eq` identifies the
order of vanishing at `C ∩ 𝔪` with the one at `𝔪`, by exhibiting `B_𝔪` as the localisation of `C`
at `C ∩ 𝔪` — the fraction `b/s` is `(g ^ k b · g ^ j)/(g ^ k · g ^ j s)` with numerator and
denominator in `C` — and `inertiaDeg_comap_eq` identifies the inertia degrees, because `C/(C ∩ 𝔪)`
is a field in which `g` is invertible, so `b = (g ^ k b) · (g^{-1}) ^ k` is congruent mod `𝔪` to an
element of `C` and `C/(C ∩ 𝔪) → B/𝔪` is onto.

## References

* [StackProject 02MM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MM)
* [StackProject 02MA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MA)
* [StackProject 02MJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MJ)
* [StackProject 00QB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QB)
-/

namespace Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.DegreeInequality

open Polynomial

/-- In an algebraic extension of domains a prime contracting to the zero ideal is the zero ideal.
This is `Ideal.eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot` with `Algebra.IsIntegral` weakened to
`Algebra.IsAlgebraic`: only the trailing coefficient of an algebraic relation is used, and it
need not be a unit. -/
private theorem eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot_of_isAlgebraic {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B] {q : Ideal B}
    (hq : q.comap (algebraMap A B) = ⊥) : q = ⊥ := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun b hb => ?_) bot_le
  simp only [Ideal.mem_bot]
  by_contra hb0
  obtain ⟨p, hp0, hp⟩ := Algebra.IsAlgebraic.isAlgebraic (R := A) b
  obtain ⟨n, g, hgc, hg⟩ : ∃ (n : ℕ) (g : A[X]), g.coeff 0 ≠ 0 ∧ p = X ^ n * g := by
    set m := p.natTrailingDegree with hm
    obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : (X : A[X]) ^ m ∣ p :=
      Polynomial.X_pow_dvd_iff.2 fun d hd => Polynomial.coeff_eq_zero_of_lt_natTrailingDegree hd
    refine ⟨m, g, ?_, hg⟩
    have h1 : p.coeff m = g.coeff 0 := by
      rw [hg]; simpa using Polynomial.coeff_X_pow_mul g m 0
    rw [← h1, hm]
    exact Polynomial.coeff_natTrailingDegree_ne_zero.2 hp0
  have hgb : (Polynomial.aeval b) g = 0 := by
    have h : b ^ n * (Polynomial.aeval b) g = 0 := by
      rw [← hp, hg]
      simp
    rcases mul_eq_zero.1 h with h | h
    · exact absurd (pow_eq_zero_iff' .. |>.1 h).1 hb0
    · exact h
  have h2 : b * (Polynomial.aeval b) g.divX + algebraMap A B (g.coeff 0) = 0 := by
    have h5 := congrArg (Polynomial.aeval b) (Polynomial.X_mul_divX_add g)
    simp only [map_add, map_mul, Polynomial.aeval_X, Polynomial.aeval_C] at h5
    exact h5.trans hgb
  have h3 : algebraMap A B (g.coeff 0) ∈ q := by
    have h4 : algebraMap A B (g.coeff 0) = -(b * (Polynomial.aeval b) g.divX) := by
      linear_combination h2
    rw [h4]
    exact neg_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hb)
  exact hgc (Ideal.mem_bot.1 (hq ▸ h3))

/-- An extension inducing a finite extension of fraction fields is algebraic. -/
private theorem isAlgebraic_of_finite_fractionField (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] (K L : Type*) [Field K] [Field L]
    [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K] [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] [Algebra A L]
    [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower A B L] [IsScalarTower A K L] [Module.Finite K L] :
    Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B := by
  have h1 : Algebra.IsAlgebraic A K := IsLocalization.isAlgebraic K (nonZeroDivisors A)
  have h3 : Algebra.IsAlgebraic A L := Algebra.IsAlgebraic.trans A K L
  exact Algebra.IsAlgebraic.tower_bot_of_injective (S := B)
    (FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective B L)

/-- In a local domain of Krull dimension at most one which is not a field, the maximal ideal has
height one. -/
private theorem height_maximalIdeal_eq_one (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] (hA : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ≠ ⊥) :
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).height = 1 := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · have h : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).height ≤ ((1 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) := by
      rw [Ideal.height_le_iff]
      intro q hq hlt
      have hq0 : q = ⊥ := by
        by_contra h
        exact absurd ((Ideal.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot (I := q) h).eq_of_le
          (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).ne_top hlt.le) hlt.ne
      subst hq0
      simp [Ideal.height_bot]
    simpa using h
  · have h := Ideal.height_add_one_le_of_lt_of_isPrime (I := (⊥ : Ideal A))
      (J := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (Ne.lt_of_le (Ne.symm hA) bot_le)
    simpa using h

/-- The maximal ideals of `B` are the zero ideal together with the primes lying over `𝔪_A`. -/
private theorem isMaximal_subset_insert_bot_primesOver {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [IsLocalRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A]
    [Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B] :
    {I : Ideal B | I.IsMaximal} ⊆ insert ⊥ ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).primesOver B) := by
  intro I hI
  have hIp : I.IsPrime := Ideal.IsMaximal.isPrime hI
  have : (I.comap (algebraMap A B)).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  by_cases h0 : I.comap (algebraMap A B) = ⊥
  · exact Set.mem_insert_iff.2 (Or.inl (eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot_of_isAlgebraic h0))
  · refine Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ ⟨hIp, ⟨?_⟩⟩
    exact ((Ideal.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot _ h0).eq_of_le
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).ne_top
      (IsLocalRing.le_maximalIdeal (Ideal.IsPrime.ne_top ‹_›))).symm

/-- An algebraic extension of finite type of a local Noetherian domain of dimension at most one
is quasi-finite: the fibre over `(0)` is the single prime `(0)`, by
`eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot_of_isAlgebraic`, and the fibre over the maximal ideal is finite by
Stacks 02MA, the maximal ideal having height one. -/
private theorem quasiFinite_of_isAlgebraic {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
    [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B] :
    Algebra.QuasiFinite A B := by
  rw [Algebra.QuasiFinite.iff_finite_primesOver]
  intro I hI
  have := hI
  by_cases h0 : I = ⊥
  · refine Set.Finite.subset (Set.finite_singleton (⊥ : Ideal B)) fun q hq => ?_
    refine Set.mem_singleton_iff.2 (eq_bot_of_comap_eq_bot_of_isAlgebraic (A := A) ?_)
    have h : I = Ideal.under A q := hq.2.over
    rw [h0] at h
    exact h.symm
  · have hIm : I = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A :=
      IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot I h0)
    rw [hIm] at h0 ⊢
    exact (Ideal.primesOver_finite_and_forall_height_eq_one _ B
      (height_maximalIdeal_eq_one A h0)).1

/-- **Semi-locality.** An extension of domains `A ⊆ B` with `A` local Noetherian of Krull
dimension at most one and `B` algebraic and of finite type over `A` has only finitely many
maximal ideals. -/
private theorem finite_maximalSpectrum {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
    [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B] :
    Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) := by
  have hfin : ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A).primesOver B).Finite :=
    Algebra.QuasiFinite.iff_finite_primesOver.1 quasiFinite_of_isAlgebraic _ inferInstance
  have hfin2 : {I : Ideal B | I.IsMaximal}.Finite :=
    (hfin.insert ⊥).subset isMaximal_subset_insert_bot_primesOver
  have : Finite {I : Ideal B // I ∈ {I : Ideal B | I.IsMaximal}} := hfin2.to_subtype
  refine Finite.of_injective
    (fun m : MaximalSpectrum B => (⟨m.asIdeal, m.isMaximal⟩ :
      {I : Ideal B // I ∈ {I : Ideal B | I.IsMaximal}})) fun m n h => ?_
  exact MaximalSpectrum.ext (congrArg Subtype.val h)

/-- An element that is not a unit has nonzero order of vanishing. -/
private theorem ord_ne_zero_of_not_isUnit {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {y : R} (hy : ¬ IsUnit y) :
    Ring.ord R y ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  have hs : Subsingleton (R ⧸ Ideal.span {y}) := Module.length_eq_zero_iff.mp h0
  refine hy (Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mp ?_)
  rw [Ideal.eq_top_iff_one, ← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

/-- **Zariski's main theorem in the form used here** (Stacks 00QB). There is a finite
`A`-subalgebra `C ⊆ B` such that every maximal ideal `𝔪` of `B` admits `g ∈ C` with `g ∉ 𝔪` and
`B ⊆ C[1/g]`. Everything the proof of Stacks 02MM needs about `C` follows from this one
statement: the contraction `𝔫 = C ∩ 𝔪` then has `C_𝔫 = B_𝔪` and `C/𝔫 = B/𝔪`, and the map
`𝔪 ↦ C ∩ 𝔪` is injective. -/
private theorem exists_finite_subalgebra_forall_isMaximal {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B]
    [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B] :
    ∃ C : Subalgebra A B, Module.Finite A C ∧
      ∀ m : Ideal B, m.IsMaximal → ∃ g : C, (g : B) ∉ m ∧
        ∀ b : B, ∃ k : ℕ, (g : B) ^ k * b ∈ C := by
  have : Algebra.QuasiFinite A B := quasiFinite_of_isAlgebraic
  obtain ⟨C, -, hCfin, hopen, haway⟩ := quasiFinite_exists_finite_subalgebra (R := A) (S := B)
  refine ⟨C, hCfin, fun m hm => ?_⟩
  have := hm.isPrime
  set q : PrimeSpectrum B := ⟨m, hm.isPrime⟩ with hq
  obtain ⟨V, hVb, hnV, hVsub⟩ :=
    PrimeSpectrum.isTopologicalBasis_basic_opens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
      (a := PrimeSpectrum.comap C.val.toRingHom q)
      (u := Set.range (PrimeSpectrum.comap C.val.toRingHom)) ⟨q, rfl⟩ hopen.isOpen_range
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := hVb
  have hgm : (g : B) ∉ m := (PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen _ _).1 hnV
  refine ⟨g, hgm, fun b => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := (haway g hVsub).2
    (algebraMap B (Localization.Away (C.val.toRingHom g)) b)
  obtain ⟨j, a, hja⟩ := IsLocalization.Away.surj (g : C) z
  have hcompat : ∀ w : C, Localization.awayMap C.val.toRingHom g
      (algebraMap C (Localization.Away g) w)
      = algebraMap B (Localization.Away (C.val.toRingHom g)) (C.val w) := by
    intro w
    rw [Localization.awayMap, IsLocalization.Away.map, IsLocalization.map_eq]; rfl
  have happ := congrArg (Localization.awayMap C.val.toRingHom g) hja
  rw [map_mul, map_pow, hz, hcompat, hcompat] at happ
  have heq : algebraMap B (Localization.Away (C.val.toRingHom g)) (C.val g ^ j * b)
      = algebraMap B (Localization.Away (C.val.toRingHom g)) (C.val a) := by
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, ← happ]
    ring
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := IsLocalization.exists_of_eq (M := Submonoid.powers (C.val.toRingHom g)) heq
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := c.2
  refine ⟨i + j, ?_⟩
  have hfinal : C.val g ^ (i + j) * b = C.val g ^ i * C.val a := by
    rw [← hi] at hc
    calc C.val g ^ (i + j) * b = C.val g ^ i * (C.val g ^ j * b) := by ring
      _ = C.val g ^ i * C.val a := hc
  change C.val g ^ (i + j) * b ∈ C
  rw [hfinal]
  exact mul_mem (pow_mem g.2 i) a.2

/-- The order of vanishing of an element of `C` is the same in `C_{C ∩ 𝔪}` and in `B_𝔪`. -/
private theorem ord_localization_comap_eq {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B]
    [Algebra A B] (C : Subalgebra A B) (m : Ideal B) [hm : m.IsPrime]
    (g : C) (hg : (g : B) ∉ m) (hgb : ∀ b : B, ∃ k : ℕ, (g : B) ^ k * b ∈ C) (y : C) :
    Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
        (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B))) y)
      = Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m) (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m) (y : B)) := by
  have : (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  let algC : Algebra C (Localization.AtPrime m) :=
    ((algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m)).comp (C.val : C →+* B)).toAlgebra
  have hmap : ∀ c : C, algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime m) c
      = algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m) (c : B) := fun _ => rfl
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m)) :=
    IsLocalization.injective _ m.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have : IsLocalization (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime m) := by
    refine ⟨fun s => ?_, fun z => ?_, fun {c c'} h => ?_⟩
    · rw [hmap]
      exact IsLocalization.map_units (M := m.primeCompl) _ ⟨(s : B), s.2⟩
    · obtain ⟨⟨b, s⟩, hbs⟩ := IsLocalization.surj (M := m.primeCompl) z
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgb b
      obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hgb (s : B)
      refine ⟨⟨⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ * g ^ j, ⟨⟨(g : B) ^ j * (s : B), hj⟩ * g ^ k, ?_⟩⟩, ?_⟩
      · simp only [Ideal.primeCompl, Submonoid.mem_mk]
        intro hmem
        have hh : (g : B) ^ j * (s : B) * (g : B) ^ k ∈ m := hmem
        rcases hm.mem_or_mem hh with h1 | h2
        · rcases hm.mem_or_mem h1 with h3 | h4
          · exact hg (hm.mem_of_pow_mem j h3)
          · exact s.2 h4
        · exact hg (hm.mem_of_pow_mem k h2)
      · rw [hmap, hmap]
        simp only [Subalgebra.coe_mul, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, map_mul]
        linear_combination (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m) ((g : B) ^ j)
          * algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m) ((g : B) ^ k)) * hbs
    · exact ⟨1, by rw [Subtype.ext (hinj ((hmap c).symm.trans (h.trans (hmap c'))))]⟩
  have e := IsLocalization.algEquiv (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).primeCompl
    (Localization.AtPrime (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B))) (Localization.AtPrime m)
  rw [Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.ord_eq_of_ringEquiv e.toRingEquiv (algebraMap C _ y)]
  congr 1
  exact e.commutes y

/-- The residue field of `C ∩ 𝔪` agrees with that of `𝔪`, so the inertia degrees agree. -/
private theorem inertiaDeg_comap_eq {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (C : Subalgebra A B) (p : Ideal A) [p.IsMaximal] (m : Ideal B) [m.IsMaximal] [m.LiesOver p]
    (g : C) (hg : (g : B) ∉ m) (hgb : ∀ b : B, ∃ k : ℕ, (g : B) ^ k * b ∈ C)
    (hn : (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).IsMaximal) :
    (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).inertiaDeg A = m.inertiaDeg A := by
  have hab : (C.val : C →+* B).comp (algebraMap A C) = algebraMap A B := RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl
  have hn' := hn
  have : (m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).LiesOver p :=
    ⟨by rw [Ideal.under_def, Ideal.comap_comap, hab]; exact Ideal.LiesOver.over⟩
  rw [Ideal.inertiaDeg_eq_of_isMaximal p, Ideal.inertiaDeg_eq_of_isMaximal p]
  -- `g` is invertible modulo `C ∩ 𝔪`, since that ideal is maximal and misses `g`
  have htop : m.comap (C.val : C →+* B) ⊔ Ideal.span {g} = ⊤ := by
    by_contra hcon
    have heq := hn.eq_of_le hcon le_sup_left
    have hmem : g ∈ m.comap (C.val : C →+* B) ⊔ Ideal.span {g} :=
      (le_sup_right : Ideal.span {g} ≤ _) (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self g)
    rw [← heq] at hmem
    exact hg hmem
  obtain ⟨n, hn1, y, hy, hsum⟩ :=
    Submodule.mem_sup.1 (htop.ge (Submodule.mem_top : (1 : C) ∈ ⊤))
  obtain ⟨c₀, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hy
  have hGZ : (Ideal.Quotient.mk m (c₀ : B)) * (Ideal.Quotient.mk m (g : B)) = 1 := by
    have h3 : (n : B) + (c₀ : B) * (g : B) = 1 := by
      have := congrArg (fun z : C => (z : B)) hsum
      push_cast at this
      exact this
    have h4 : (n : B) ∈ m := hn1
    have h5 := (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem (I := m)).2 h4
    have h6 := congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk m) h3
    rw [map_add, map_mul, map_one, h5, zero_add] at h6
    exact h6
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (Ideal.quotientMap m (C.val : C →+* B) le_rfl) := by
    intro w
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective w
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgb b
    refine ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ((⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) * c₀ ^ k), ?_⟩
    rw [Ideal.quotientMap_mk]
    have hcast : (C.val : C →+* B) ((⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) * c₀ ^ k)
        = (g : B) ^ k * b * (c₀ : B) ^ k := by push_cast; rfl
    rw [hcast, map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow]
    calc Ideal.Quotient.mk m (g : B) ^ k * Ideal.Quotient.mk m b
          * Ideal.Quotient.mk m (c₀ : B) ^ k
        = (Ideal.Quotient.mk m (c₀ : B) * Ideal.Quotient.mk m (g : B)) ^ k
          * Ideal.Quotient.mk m b := by rw [mul_pow]; ring
      _ = Ideal.Quotient.mk m b := by rw [hGZ, one_pow, one_mul]
  have ea : (C ⧸ m.comap (C.val : C →+* B)) ≃ₐ[A ⧸ p] (B ⧸ m) :=
    AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := RingEquiv.ofBijective
        (Ideal.quotientMap m (C.val : C →+* B) le_rfl)
        ⟨Ideal.quotientMap_injective, hsurj⟩)
      (fun r => by obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective r; rfl)
  exact ea.toLinearEquiv.finrank_eq

/-- The order of vanishing at a prime of an element outside it is zero: the element becomes a
unit in the localisation. -/
private theorem ord_localization_eq_zero_of_notMem {B : Type*} [CommRing B] (m : Ideal B)
    [m.IsPrime] {b : B} (hb : b ∉ m) :
    Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m) (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m) b) = 0 :=
  Ring.ord_of_isUnit (IsLocalization.map_units (M := m.primeCompl) _ ⟨b, hb⟩)

/-- If some `g` in a subalgebra `C ⊆ B` carries every element of `B` into `C` after
multiplication by a power of `g`, then `C` has the same field of fractions as `B`: the fraction
`b / s` is `(g ^ k b · g ^ j) / (g ^ j s · g ^ k)` with numerator and denominator in `C`. -/
private theorem isFractionRing_of_forall_exists_pow_mul_mem {A B : Type*} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B] (C : Subalgebra A B) {L : Type*} [Field L]
    [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] {g : C} (hg0 : (g : B) ≠ 0)
    (hgb : ∀ b : B, ∃ k : ℕ, (g : B) ^ k * b ∈ C) :
    IsFractionRing C L := by
  have hcomp : (algebraMap C L) = (algebraMap B L).comp (C.val : C →+* B) := rfl
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap C L) := by
    rw [hcomp]
    exact (IsFractionRing.injective B L).comp Subtype.val_injective
  have : FaithfulSMul C L := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective C L).mpr hinj
  refine IsFractionRing.of_field C L fun z => ?_
  obtain ⟨b, t, ht, hz⟩ := IsFractionRing.div_surjective B z
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgb b
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := hgb t
  refine ⟨(⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) * g ^ j, (⟨(g : B) ^ j * t, hj⟩ : C) * g ^ k, ?_⟩
  have hval1 : (((⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) * g ^ j : C) : B)
      = (g : B) ^ k * b * (g : B) ^ j := by push_cast; rfl
  have hval2 : (((⟨(g : B) ^ j * t, hj⟩ : C) * g ^ k : C) : B)
      = (g : B) ^ j * t * (g : B) ^ k := by push_cast; rfl
  have htne : algebraMap B L t ≠ 0 := by
    simpa using (IsFractionRing.injective B L).ne (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero ht)
  have hgne : algebraMap B L (g : B) ≠ 0 := by
    simpa using (IsFractionRing.injective B L).ne hg0
  rw [← hz, hcomp]
  simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply]
  rw [show ((C.val : C →+* B)) ((⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) * g ^ j)
      = (g : B) ^ k * b * (g : B) ^ j from hval1,
    show ((C.val : C →+* B)) ((⟨(g : B) ^ j * t, hj⟩ : C) * g ^ k)
      = (g : B) ^ j * t * (g : B) ^ k from hval2,
    div_eq_div_iff htne (by simp [map_mul, map_pow, htne, hgne])]
  simp only [map_mul, map_pow]
  ring

/-- Every prime of a module-finite extension `C` of a local ring `A` lying over the maximal ideal
of `A` contributes a nonzero term to the count of Stacks 02MJ: the inertia degree of a prime of a
module-finite extension is positive, and an element of the maximal ideal of `A` is a non-unit in
the localisation of `C` at such a prime. -/
private theorem inertiaDeg_mul_ord_ne_zero {A C : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Module.Finite A C] (n : Ideal C) [n.IsPrime]
    [n.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)] {x : A} (hx : x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :
    (n.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n)
        (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n) (algebraMap A C x)) ≠ 0 := by
  rw [Ne, mul_eq_zero, not_or]
  refine ⟨by exact_mod_cast (Ideal.inertiaDeg_pos n A).ne', ord_ne_zero_of_not_isUnit ?_⟩
  have hmem : algebraMap A C x ∈ n := show x ∈ n.comap (algebraMap A C) by
    rw [← Ideal.under_def, ← Ideal.LiesOver.over (p := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (P := n)]
    exact hx
  rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.isUnit_to_map_iff (Localization.AtPrime n) n]
  exact fun h => h hmem

/-- A finite sum in `ℕ∞` along an injection is at most the total sum, and equals it only if the
injection is surjective, provided every term is nonzero and finite. -/
private theorem sum_comp_le_and_surjective_of_eq {α β : Type*} [Fintype α] [Fintype β]
    (Φ : α → β) (hΦ : Function.Injective Φ) (G : β → ℕ∞) (hG0 : ∀ b, G b ≠ 0)
    (hGtop : ∀ b, G b ≠ ⊤) :
    ∑ a, G (Φ a) ≤ ∑ b, G b ∧ (∑ a, G (Φ a) = ∑ b, G b → Function.Surjective Φ) := by
  classical
  have himg : ∑ b ∈ Finset.image Φ Finset.univ, G b = ∑ a, G (Φ a) :=
    Finset.sum_image fun a _ a' _ h => hΦ h
  have hsplit := Finset.sum_sdiff (f := G) (Finset.subset_univ (Finset.image Φ Finset.univ))
  have hne : ∀ s : Finset β, (∑ b ∈ s, G b) ≠ ⊤ :=
    fun s => ENat.sum_ne_top.mpr fun b _ => hGtop b
  refine ⟨?_, fun heq => ?_⟩
  · rw [← himg, ← hsplit]
    exact le_add_self
  · rw [← himg, ← hsplit] at heq
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ : ∃ p : ℕ, ∑ b ∈ Finset.univ \ Finset.image Φ Finset.univ, G b = (p : ℕ∞) :=
      ⟨_, (ENat.natCast_toNat (hne _)).symm⟩
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ : ∃ q : ℕ, ∑ b ∈ Finset.image Φ Finset.univ, G b = (q : ℕ∞) :=
      ⟨_, (ENat.natCast_toNat (hne _)).symm⟩
    rw [hp, hq, ← Nat.cast_add, Nat.cast_inj] at heq
    have hzero : ∑ b ∈ Finset.univ \ Finset.image Φ Finset.univ, G b = 0 := by
      rw [hp, show p = 0 by omega, Nat.cast_zero]
    intro b
    by_contra hb
    refine hG0 b (Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff.mp hzero b ?_)
    simpa using hb

/-- A maximal ideal of an integral extension of a local ring lies over the maximal ideal. -/
private theorem liesOver_maximalIdeal_of_isIntegral {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra.IsIntegral A B] (m : Ideal B) [m.IsMaximal] :
    m.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
  ⟨(IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal
    (Ideal.isMaximal_under_of_isIntegral_of_isMaximal (R := A) m)).symm⟩

set_option linter.deprecated false in
/-- **The norm formula for a finite extension.** For `A ⊆ B` a finite extension of domains with
`A` local Noetherian of Krull dimension at most one, and `x` a nonzero element of `A`, the sum
over the maximal ideals `𝔪` of `B` of `[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x)` equals `[L : K] · ord_A(x)`.

This is `ord_norm_eq_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord` (Stacks 02MJ) at `y = x`, whose norm is
`x ^ [L : K]`. -/
private theorem sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B]
    [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] [Module.Finite A B] [Finite (MaximalSpectrum B)]
    {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L]
    [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K] [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] [Algebra A L]
    [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower A B L] [IsScalarTower A K L] [Module.Finite K L]
    (x : A) (hx0 : x ≠ 0) :
    ∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
      = (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x := by
  classical
  have hinjAB : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B) := FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective A B
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral A B := Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite A B
  have : Ring.DimensionLEOne A := ⟨fun {p} hp _ => Ideal.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot p hp⟩
  have : Ring.DimensionLEOne B := Ring.DimensionLEOne.of_isIntegral (R := A) B
  have hNB : IsNoetherianRing B := IsNoetherianRing.of_finite A B
  have hfB : Fintype (MaximalSpectrum B) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  -- The localisations `B_𝔪` sit inside `L` as the localisations of `B` at larger submonoids.
  let algL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, Algebra (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L := fun v =>
    IsLocalization.localizationAlgebraOfSubmonoidLe _ _ v.asIdeal.primeCompl (nonZeroDivisors B)
      v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have towL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, IsScalarTower B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
    fun v => IsLocalization.localization_isScalarTower_of_submonoid_le _ _
      v.asIdeal.primeCompl (nonZeroDivisors B) v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have fracL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, IsFractionRing (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
    fun v => IsFractionRing.isFractionRing_of_isDomain_of_isLocalization v.asIdeal.primeCompl _ _
  have kdL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) := by
    intro v
    rw [Ring.krullDimLE_iff, IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height v.asIdeal]
    exact le_trans Ideal.height_le_ringKrullDim_of_isPrime
      (Ring.krullDimLE_iff.mp (inferInstance : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 B))
  set n := Module.finrank K L with hn
  -- Every maximal ideal of `B` lies over `𝔪_A`, since `B` is integral over `A`.
  have hlies : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, v.asIdeal.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) := by
    intro v
    have := v.isMaximal
    exact liesOver_maximalIdeal_of_isIntegral v.asIdeal
  have hxK : algebraMap A K x ≠ 0 := fun h =>
    hx0 ((IsFractionRing.to_map_eq_zero_iff (R := A) (K := K)).mp h)
  have hy : algebraMap A L x ≠ 0 := by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A K L x]
    exact fun h => hxK ((algebraMap K L).injective (by rw [h, map_zero]))
  have hnorm : algebraMap A K (x ^ n) = Algebra.norm K (algebraMap A L x) := by
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A K L x, Algebra.norm_algebraMap, map_pow]
  have hxKn : algebraMap A K (x ^ n) ≠ 0 := by rw [map_pow]; exact pow_ne_zero _ hxK
  have key := ord_norm_eq_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord A B K L hinjAB
    (algebraMap A L x) hy (algebraMap A K (x ^ n)) hnorm hxKn
  rw [ordInt_algebraMap A (x ^ n) (pow_ne_zero _ hx0) hxKn] at key
  -- Both sides of Stacks 02MJ are finite, so the identity descends from `ℤ` to `ℕ` and up to `ℕ∞`.
  have hordA : Ring.ord A x ≠ ⊤ := Ring.ord_ne_top (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hx0)
  set b := (Ring.ord A x).toNat with hb
  have hordAeq : Ring.ord A x = (b : ℕ∞) := (ENat.natCast_toNat hordA).symm
  have hLHS : (Module.length A (A ⧸ Ideal.span {x ^ n})).toNat = n * b := by
    have h1 : Module.length A (A ⧸ Ideal.span {x ^ n}) = Ring.ord A (x ^ n) := rfl
    rw [h1, Ring.ord_pow (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hx0), hordAeq]
    rw [nsmul_eq_mul, ← Nat.cast_mul, ENat.toNat_natCast]
  have hbvne : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B,
      algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x) ≠ 0 := by
    intro v h
    have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal)) :=
      IsLocalization.injective _ v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
    have h2 : algebraMap A B x = 0 := hinj (by rw [h, map_zero])
    exact hx0 (hinjAB (by rw [h2, map_zero]))
  have hstep : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B,
      ordInt (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A L x) hy
        = ((Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal)
            (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))).toNat : ℤ) := by
    intro v
    have he : algebraMap A L x
        = algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L
            (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x)) := by
      rw [← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L,
        ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A B L]
    have hcongr : ∀ (a a' : L) (ha : a ≠ 0) (ha' : a' ≠ 0), a = a' →
        ordInt (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) a ha
          = ordInt (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) a' ha' := by
      intro a a' ha ha' h; subst h; rfl
    rw [hcongr _ _ hy (he ▸ hy) he,
      ordInt_algebraMap (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) _ (hbvne v) (he ▸ hy)]
    rfl
  have hdeg : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B,
      Ideal.inertiaDeg' (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) v.asIdeal = v.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A := by
    intro v
    have h1 := hlies v
    have h2 := v.isMaximal
    exact Ideal.inertiaDeg'_eq_inertiaDeg _ _
  rw [hLHS] at key
  simp only [hstep, hdeg] at key
  have keyN : n * b = ∑ v : MaximalSpectrum B, v.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A *
      (Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal)
        (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))).toNat := by
    exact_mod_cast key
  have hordv : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B,
      Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
        = (((Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal)
            (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))).toNat : ℕ) : ℕ∞) :=
    fun v => (ENat.natCast_toNat
      (Ring.ord_ne_top (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero (hbvne v)))).symm
  rw [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype, hordAeq, ← Nat.cast_mul, keyN, Nat.cast_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun v _ => by rw [hordv v, Nat.cast_mul, ENat.toNat_natCast]

/-- **The degree inequality, and finiteness as the case of equality.** For `A ⊆ B` an extension of
domains with `A` local Noetherian of Krull dimension at most one, `B` of finite type over `A` and
the induced extension `L/K` of fraction fields finite, and for `x` a nonzero element of the maximal
ideal of `A`, the sum over the maximal ideals `𝔪` of `B` of `[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x)` is at
most `[L : K] · ord_A(x)`, and equality forces `A → B` to be finite.

The two halves come out of one construction, so they are proved together. If `(0)` is a maximal
ideal of `B` it is the only one, `x` is a unit there, and the left side is `0` while the right side
is not: the inequality is trivial and equality impossible. Otherwise every maximal ideal of `B`
lies over `𝔪_A`, and the finite `A`-subalgebra `C ⊆ B` of
`exists_finite_subalgebra_forall_isMaximal` has `L` for its field of fractions
(`isFractionRing_of_forall_exists_pow_mul_mem`) and the same term at `C ∩ 𝔪` as `B` has at `𝔪`
(`ord_localization_comap_eq` and `inertiaDeg_comap_eq`). The left side is therefore a subsum, along
the injection `𝔪 ↦ C ∩ 𝔪`, of the exact count `sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite` for `C`; every
term of that count is nonzero (`inertiaDeg_mul_ord_ne_zero`), so equality makes the injection onto
(`sum_comp_le_and_surjective_of_eq`), and then for `b ∈ B` the ideal `{c ∈ C | c b ∈ C}` of `C`
lies in no maximal ideal of `C` and is `C` itself, whence `b ∈ C` and `C = B`. -/
private theorem sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_finite_of_eq {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B]
    [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L]
    [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K] [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] [Algebra A L]
    [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower A B L] [IsScalarTower A K L] [Module.Finite K L]
    (x : A) (hx : x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (hx0 : x ≠ 0) :
    (∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
          Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
            (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
        ≤ (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) ∧
      ((∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
              (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
          = (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) → Module.Finite A B) := by
  classical
  have : Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B := isAlgebraic_of_finite_fractionField A B K L
  have : Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) := finite_maximalSpectrum (A := A)
  have : Fintype (MaximalSpectrum B) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  have hinjAB : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B) := FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective A B
  have hRHS : (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x ≠ 0 := by
    rw [Ne, mul_eq_zero, not_or]
    exact ⟨by exact_mod_cast Module.finrank_pos.ne',
      ord_ne_zero_of_not_isUnit ((IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal x).mp hx)⟩
  rw [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype]
  by_cases hbot : ∃ m : MaximalSpectrum B, m.asIdeal = ⊥
  · -- `(0)` is then the only maximal ideal of `B`, and `x` is a unit in the localisation there.
    obtain ⟨m₀, hm₀⟩ := hbot
    have hsum : ∑ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x)) = 0 := by
      refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun m _ => ?_
      have : m.asIdeal.IsPrime := m.isMaximal.isPrime
      have hbotmax : (⊥ : Ideal B).IsMaximal := hm₀ ▸ m₀.isMaximal
      have hmb : m.asIdeal = ⊥ := (hbotmax.eq_of_le m.isMaximal.ne_top bot_le).symm
      have hnm : algebraMap A B x ∉ m.asIdeal := by
        rw [hmb, Ideal.mem_bot]
        exact fun h => hx0 (hinjAB (by rw [h, map_zero]))
      rw [ord_localization_eq_zero_of_notMem m.asIdeal hnm, mul_zero]
    exact ⟨hsum.trans_le zero_le, fun h => absurd (h.symm.trans hsum) hRHS⟩
  · simp only [not_exists] at hbot
    -- Every maximal ideal of `B` now lies over the maximal ideal of `A`.
    have hlies : ∀ m : MaximalSpectrum B, m.asIdeal.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) := by
      intro m
      have hmem := isMaximal_subset_insert_bot_primesOver (A := A) (B := B) m.isMaximal
      rcases Set.mem_insert_iff.1 hmem with h | h
      · exact absurd h (hbot m)
      · exact h.2
    obtain ⟨C, hCfin, hC⟩ := exists_finite_subalgebra_forall_isMaximal (A := A) (B := B)
    have : Module.Finite A C := hCfin
    have : Algebra.IsIntegral A C := .of_finite _ _
    have hinjAC : Function.Injective (algebraMap A C) :=
      fun a a' h => hinjAB (congrArg (C.val : C → B) h)
    have : FaithfulSMul A C := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective A C).mpr hinjAC
    have : Finite (MaximalSpectrum C) := finite_maximalSpectrum (A := A) (B := C)
    have : Fintype (MaximalSpectrum C) := Fintype.ofFinite _
    obtain ⟨m₁, hm₁⟩ := Ideal.exists_maximal B
    obtain ⟨g₁, hg₁, hg₁b⟩ := hC m₁ hm₁
    have : IsFractionRing C L := isFractionRing_of_forall_exists_pow_mul_mem C
      (fun h => hg₁ (by rw [h]; exact Ideal.zero_mem m₁)) hg₁b
    -- The contraction of a maximal ideal of `B` is a maximal ideal of `C`.
    have hcomapmax : ∀ m : MaximalSpectrum B,
        (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).IsMaximal := by
      intro m
      have : m.asIdeal.IsPrime := m.isMaximal.isPrime
      have : (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
      refine Ideal.isMaximal_of_isIntegral_of_isMaximal_under (R := A) _ ?_
      have h1 : (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).comap (algebraMap A C)
          = m.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap A B) := by
        rw [Ideal.comap_comap]
        rfl
      have h2 : m.asIdeal.comap (algebraMap A B) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := by
        have h3 := (hlies m).over
        rw [Ideal.under_def] at h3
        exact h3.symm
      rw [Ideal.under_def, h1, h2]
      exact IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal A
    -- Distinct maximal ideals of `B` have distinct contractions.
    have hcomaple : ∀ u v : MaximalSpectrum B,
        u.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) = v.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) →
          v.asIdeal ≤ u.asIdeal := by
      intro u v huv b hb
      obtain ⟨g, hg, hgb⟩ := hC u.asIdeal u.isMaximal
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgb b
      have h1 : (⟨(g : B) ^ k * b, hk⟩ : C) ∈ v.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) := by
        rw [Ideal.mem_comap]
        exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hb
      rw [← huv, Ideal.mem_comap] at h1
      have h3 : (g : B) ^ k * b ∈ u.asIdeal := h1
      have hp : u.asIdeal.IsPrime := u.isMaximal.isPrime
      rcases hp.mem_or_mem h3 with h4 | h5
      · exact absurd (hp.mem_of_pow_mem k h4) hg
      · exact h5
    have hΦinj : Function.Injective (fun m : MaximalSpectrum B =>
        (⟨m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B), hcomapmax m⟩ : MaximalSpectrum C)) := by
      intro u v huv
      have h : u.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) = v.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) :=
        congrArg MaximalSpectrum.asIdeal huv
      exact MaximalSpectrum.ext (le_antisymm (hcomaple v u h.symm) (hcomaple u v h))
    -- The term of `C` at the contraction is the term of `B`.
    have hterm : ∀ m : MaximalSpectrum B,
        ((m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
              (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
                (algebraMap A C x))
          = (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
              (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x)) := by
      intro m
      have := m.isMaximal
      have := hlies m
      have : m.asIdeal.IsPrime := m.isMaximal.isPrime
      obtain ⟨g, hg, hgb⟩ := hC m.asIdeal m.isMaximal
      have hcast : ((algebraMap A C x : C) : B) = algebraMap A B x := rfl
      rw [inertiaDeg_comap_eq C (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) m.asIdeal g hg hgb (hcomapmax m),
        ord_localization_comap_eq C m.asIdeal g hg hgb (algebraMap A C x), hcast]
    -- Stacks 02MJ for `C`, and the two finiteness facts its right-hand side gives.
    have hCsum := sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite (A := A) (B := C) (K := K) (L := L) x hx0
    rw [finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype] at hCsum
    have hordA : Ring.ord A x ≠ ⊤ := Ring.ord_ne_top (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hx0)
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ : ∃ p : ℕ, Ring.ord A x = (p : ℕ∞) := ⟨_, (ENat.natCast_toNat hordA).symm⟩
    have htot : (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x ≠ ⊤ := by
      rw [hp, ← Nat.cast_mul]
      exact ENat.natCast_ne_top _
    have hG0 : ∀ n : MaximalSpectrum C, (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x)) ≠ 0 := by
      intro n
      have := n.isMaximal
      have : n.asIdeal.IsPrime := n.isMaximal.isPrime
      have : n.asIdeal.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
        liesOver_maximalIdeal_of_isIntegral n.asIdeal
      exact inertiaDeg_mul_ord_ne_zero n.asIdeal hx
    have hsumtop : ∑ n : MaximalSpectrum C, (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
      rw [hCsum]
      exact htot
    have hGtop : ∀ n : MaximalSpectrum C, (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
      intro n
      refine ne_top_of_le_ne_top hsumtop ?_
      exact Finset.single_le_sum
        (f := fun n : MaximalSpectrum C => (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
          Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
            (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x)))
        (fun n _ => zero_le) (Finset.mem_univ n)
    obtain ⟨hle, hsurj⟩ := sum_comp_le_and_surjective_of_eq
      (fun m : MaximalSpectrum B =>
        (⟨m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B), hcomapmax m⟩ : MaximalSpectrum C)) hΦinj
      (fun n : MaximalSpectrum C => (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
        Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
          (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x))) hG0 hGtop
    have hFG : ∑ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
          Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
            (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
        = ∑ m : MaximalSpectrum B,
          ((m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
              (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
                (algebraMap A C x)) :=
      Finset.sum_congr rfl fun m _ => (hterm m).symm
    refine ⟨by rw [hFG]; exact le_trans hle (le_of_eq hCsum), fun heq => ?_⟩
    -- Equality makes `𝔪 ↦ C ∩ 𝔪` onto, and then `C = B`.
    have heq2 : ∑ m : MaximalSpectrum B,
          ((m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)).inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
              (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime (m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B)))
                (algebraMap A C x))
        = ∑ n : MaximalSpectrum C, (n.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
            Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal)
              (algebraMap C (Localization.AtPrime n.asIdeal) (algebraMap A C x)) := by
      rw [← hFG, heq, ← hCsum]
    have hΦsurj := hsurj heq2
    have hCtop : C = ⊤ := by
      refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun b _ => ?_
      let I : Ideal C :=
        { carrier := {c : C | (c : B) * b ∈ C}
          add_mem' := fun {c d} hc hd => by
            simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hc hd ⊢
            have h : ((c + d : C) : B) * b = (c : B) * b + (d : B) * b := by push_cast; ring
            rw [h]
            exact add_mem hc hd
          zero_mem' := by simp
          smul_mem' := fun c {d} hd => by
            simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hd ⊢
            have h : ((c • d : C) : B) * b = (c : B) * ((d : B) * b) := by
              push_cast [smul_eq_mul]; ring
            rw [h]
            exact mul_mem c.2 hd }
      have hItop : I = ⊤ := by
        by_contra hI
        obtain ⟨n, hn, hIn⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal I hI
        obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hΦsurj ⟨n, hn⟩
        obtain ⟨g, hg, hgb⟩ := hC m.asIdeal m.isMaximal
        obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgb b
        have hgI : (g ^ k : C) ∈ I :=
          show ((g ^ k : C) : B) * b ∈ C by push_cast; exact hk
        have hgn : (g ^ k : C) ∈ n := hIn hgI
        have hncomap : n = m.asIdeal.comap (C.val : C →+* B) :=
          (congrArg MaximalSpectrum.asIdeal hm).symm
        have hmem : g ∈ n := hn.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem k hgn
        rw [hncomap, Ideal.mem_comap] at hmem
        exact hg hmem
      have h1 : (1 : C) ∈ I := hItop ▸ Submodule.mem_top
      have h2 : ((1 : C) : B) * b ∈ C := h1
      simpa using h2
    have hfin2 : Module.Finite A (⊤ : Subalgebra A B) := hCtop ▸ hCfin
    exact Module.Finite.equiv (Subalgebra.topEquiv (R := A) (A := B)).toLinearEquiv

/-- The degree inequality for orders of vanishing (Stacks 02MM): for `A ⊆ B` an extension of
domains with `A` local Noetherian of dimension at most `1`, `B` of finite type over `A` and `L/K`
finite, `B` is semi-local, and for every nonzero `x` in the maximal ideal of `A` the sum over the
maximal ideals `𝔪` of `B` of `[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x)` is at most `[L : K] · ord_A(x)`,
with equality if and only if `A → B` is finite. -/
public theorem solution
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B]
    [Algebra.FiniteType A B] {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] [Algebra A L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower A B L]
    [IsScalarTower A K L] [Module.Finite K L] :
    Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, x ≠ 0 →
        (∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
              Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
                (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
            ≤ (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) ∧
          ((∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
                Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
                  (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
              = (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) ↔ Module.Finite A B) := by
  have : Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B := isAlgebraic_of_finite_fractionField A B K L
  have hfin : Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) := finite_maximalSpectrum (A := A)
  refine ⟨hfin, fun x hx hx0 => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨hle, hfinite⟩ :=
    sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_finite_of_eq (A := A) (B := B) (K := K) (L := L) x hx hx0
  exact ⟨hle, hfinite, fun _ => sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_eq_of_finite (K := K) (L := L) x hx0⟩

end Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.DegreeInequality

/-!
# The degree inequality for orders of vanishing, and finiteness as the case of equality

Let `A ⊆ B` be an extension of domains with `A` local Noetherian of dimension `1`, let `B` be of
finite type over `A`, and let `L/K` be the induced extension of fraction fields, assumed finite.
Then `B` is semi-local, and for every nonzero `x` in the maximal ideal of `A`,

`∑_𝔪 [κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x) ≤ [L : K] · ord_A(x)`,

the sum being over the maximal ideals of `B`; equality holds if and only if `A → B` is finite.

Geometrically the two sides count the fibre over the closed point of `Spec A` twice: on the right
with the multiplicity the generic fibre prescribes, on the left with the multiplicity actually
present in `B`. The defect measures the points that a generically finite morphism of finite type
has lost, and the inequality is an equality exactly when none are missing, that is when `A → B`
is finite. This is the promised characterisation of the finite maps among the quasi-finite ones,
and its proof is an application of Zariski's main theorem: the finite subalgebra `C ⊆ B` produced
there has the same localisations as `B` at the maximal ideals of `B`, together with the "missing
points", and each missing point contributes a positive term to the exact count for `C`.

## Main results

* `Ring.finite_maximalSpectrum_and_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_eq_iff_finite`: the three
  assertions of the tag — `B` is semi-local, the inequality above, and equality if and only if
  `A → B` is finite.
* `finite_maximalSpectrum_and_ordInt_norm_eq_finsum_inertiaDeg_mul_ordInt` (Stacks 02MJ): for
  `A ⊆ B` a finite extension of domains, `B` is semi-local and
  `ord_A(Nm_{L/K}(y)) = ∑ᵢ [κ(𝔪ᵢ) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_{𝔪ᵢ}}(y)`, under the source's hypotheses
  only.

## Implementation notes

The order of vanishing is Mathlib's `Ring.ord R x = Module.length R (R ⧸ (x))`, valued in `ℕ∞`
and carrying the tag of the source's definition. The source's `x` lies in `A`, hence in `B` and in
each `B_𝔪`, so only the order of vanishing of a *ring element* occurs and the extension of `ord`
to `K^*` (`Ring.ordFrac`) is not needed: the statement lives in `ℕ∞`, and in consequence it needs
no hypotheses whatever on the localisations `B_𝔪`, since `Ring.ord` has none. Every value
occurring is finite (`Ring.ord_ne_top` for the orders, the finiteness hypotheses for the degrees),
so the inequality in `ℕ∞` says what the inequality in `ℤ` would say.

The residue degree `[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)]` is `Ideal.inertiaDeg 𝔪 A`, the degree of the residue field
of `𝔪` over that of its contraction `𝔪.under A`. The source's sum presupposes that every maximal
ideal of `B` contracts to `𝔪_A`, which can fail: for `A` a discrete valuation ring and `B = K` its
fraction field the only maximal ideal of `B` is `0`, lying over `0`. The form used here is
faithful nonetheless, because such a maximal ideal contributes `0`: it misses `x`, so `x` is a unit
in `B_𝔪` and `Ring.ord_of_isUnit` applies. Over the maximal ideals that do lie over `𝔪_A` —
all of them as soon as `A → B` is finite — `Ideal.inertiaDeg 𝔪 A` is literally the source's degree.

Semi-locality of `B` is `Finite (MaximalSpectrum B)`; neither Mathlib nor this repository names the
notion. The sum is a `finsum` over that type, so that the first conjunct is what makes it the sum
of the source rather than the value `0` that `finsum` takes on an infinite support. The
localisation `B_𝔪` is the concrete `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪`; nothing is lost, as the length of a
quotient by a principal ideal transports along a ring isomorphism carrying the element to the
element, and this is the model in which the sum can be indexed by `MaximalSpectrum B`.

The source's `dim A = 1` is `Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A`, which is how Mathlib states the hypothesis of
the order of vanishing. The case `dim A = 0` is not excluded and is not degenerate nonsense: `A`
is then a field, `𝔪_A = 0` makes the numerical assertion vacuous, and `B` is a field too, so the
first conjunct still holds.

`A ⊆ B` is `FaithfulSMul A B`. It is implied by the two scalar towers (`A → L` is injective
because `A → K → L` is, and it factors through `B`), and `IsDomain A` is implied by `IsDomain B`
together with it; both are kept because they are the source's hypotheses and are what the
`IsFractionRing` API asks for, so neither costs any generality.

Faithfulness. (1) No hypothesis is dead. `Module.Finite K L` is live: for `A = k[t]_{(t)}` and
`B = A[y]` the extension `L = k(t)(y)` of `K = k(t)` is infinite, so `Module.finrank K L = 0`
and the left side is `0`, while `𝔪 = (t, y)` contributes at least `1` to the right side — and
`MaximalSpectrum B` is infinite, so the first conjunct fails as well. `x ∈ 𝔪_A` is live: for a
unit `x` both sides are `0`, so the inequality would still hold but equality would hold too,
and the criterion would be false. `x ≠ 0` is live: at `x = 0` both sides are `⊤`, since
`Ring.ord_zero` reads `ord_A(0) = Module.length A A` and a local ring of positive dimension has
infinite length, so equality would hold there for every `B`, finite over `A` or not.
`IsLocalRing A` is what lets `𝔪_A` be named at all.
`Algebra.FiniteType A B` is what Zariski's main theorem (Stacks 00QB) consumes and what makes `B`
semi-local (Stacks 02MA); it is not implied by `Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B`, which every
intermediate ring `A ⊆ B ⊆ L` satisfies. It and `IsNoetherianRing A` enter the proof
essentially; no claim is made here that either can be removed. (2) The scalars and the base are
the source's: `ord_A` is a length over `A`, `ord_{B_𝔪}` a length over `B_𝔪` — not over `B` and
not over `A` — the residue degree is taken over `κ(𝔪_A)`, and `[L : K]` is a rank over `K`.
(3) The canonical maps are pinned, not merely assumed to exist: `A → K` and `B → L` by
`IsFractionRing`, `K → L` as the unique `A`-algebra map extending `A → B → L` by the two scalar
towers, `B → B_𝔪` as `algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime 𝔪)`, and the residue field extension by
`Ideal.inertiaDeg`. The conclusion pins the two numbers, not merely the existence of a relation
between them. (4) The instantiation is not degenerate: for `A = ℤ_{(5)}` and `B = ℤ[i]_{(5)}`
(the localisation of `ℤ[i]` at `ℤ ∖ (5)`) with `x = 5` we have `[L : K] = 2`, `ord_A(5) = 1`, two
maximal ideals `(2 ± i)` with residue field `𝔽₅` and `ord = 1` each, so both sides are `2` and
`A → B` is finite; deleting one of the two points, `B' = B[1/(2 + i)]`, leaves the right side `1`
against the left side `2`, and `A → B'` is not finite.

## References

* [StackProject 02MM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MM)
* [StackProject 02MJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MJ)
-/

@[expose] public section

/-- **The degree inequality for orders of vanishing.** Let `A ⊆ B` be an extension of domains
with `A` local Noetherian of dimension at most `1`, `B` of finite type over `A`, and the induced
extension `L/K` of fraction fields finite. Then `B` is semi-local, and for every nonzero `x` in
the maximal ideal of `A` the sum over the maximal ideals `𝔪` of `B` of
`[κ(𝔪) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_𝔪}(x)` is at most `[L : K] · ord_A(x)`, with equality if and only if
`A → B` is finite. -/
@[stacks 02MM "`ord` is `Ring.ord`, valued in `ℕ∞`, applied to the image of `x : A`; the residue
degrees are `Ideal.inertiaDeg`; semi-locality is `Finite (MaximalSpectrum B)`; the sum is a
`finsum`. See the module docstring."]
public theorem Ring.finite_maximalSpectrum_and_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord_le_and_eq_iff_finite
    {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B] [FaithfulSMul A B]
    [Algebra.FiniteType A B] {K L : Type*} [Field K] [Field L] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L] [Algebra A L] [Algebra K L] [IsScalarTower A B L]
    [IsScalarTower A K L] [Module.Finite K L] :
    Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A, x ≠ 0 →
        (∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
              Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
                (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
            ≤ (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) ∧
          ((∑ᶠ m : MaximalSpectrum B, (m.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℕ∞) *
                Ring.ord (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal)
                  (algebraMap B (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) (algebraMap A B x))
              = (Module.finrank K L : ℕ∞) * Ring.ord A x) ↔ Module.Finite A B) :=
                by apply Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.DegreeInequality.solution

/-- The localisation `B_𝔭` of a finite extension `B` of a domain `A` of Krull dimension at most
one, at a prime `𝔭`, has Krull dimension at most one: `B` is integral over `A`, so it has
dimension at most one, and localising does not raise the dimension. -/
theorem Ring.krullDimLE_one_localization_atPrime_of_finite (A B : Type*) [CommRing A]
    [IsDomain A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain B] [Algebra A B]
    [Module.Finite A B] (p : Ideal B) [p.IsPrime] :
    Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (Localization.AtPrime p) := by
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral A B := Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite A B
  have : Ring.DimensionLEOne A := ⟨fun {p} hp _ => Ideal.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot p hp⟩
  have : Ring.DimensionLEOne B := Ring.DimensionLEOne.of_isIntegral (R := A) B
  rw [Ring.krullDimLE_iff, IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height p]
  exact le_trans Ideal.height_le_ringKrullDim_of_isPrime
    (Ring.krullDimLE_iff.mp (inferInstance : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 B))

/-- **The order of vanishing of a norm** (Stacks 02MJ). Let `A` be a Noetherian local domain of
dimension one, and let `A ⊆ B` be a finite extension of domains, with fraction fields `K ⊆ L`.
Then `B` is semi-local, with maximal ideals `𝔪₁, …, 𝔪ₙ`, and for every `y ∈ L^*` (whose norm is
nonzero, `L/K` being finite)

`ord_A(Nm_{L/K}(y)) = ∑ᵢ [κ(𝔪ᵢ) : κ(𝔪_A)] · ord_{B_{𝔪ᵢ}}(y)`.

Only the source's hypotheses are assumed. Everything the right-hand side needs is constructed
in the statement from them: `B` is Noetherian, being finite over `A`; each `B_{𝔪ᵢ}` is a
Noetherian local domain of dimension at most one; and `B_{𝔪ᵢ}` sits inside `L` as the
localisation of `B` at the larger submonoid `B ∖ {0}`, so that `L` is its fraction field and
`B → B_{𝔪ᵢ} → L` is `B → L`. -/
@[stacks 02MJ "The first conjunct is `B` being semi-local, as `Finite (MaximalSpectrum B)`. The
sum is a `finsum` over `MaximalSpectrum B`; `[κ(𝔪ᵢ) : κ(𝔪_A)]` is `Ideal.inertiaDeg 𝔪ᵢ A`, the
degree of the residue field of `𝔪ᵢ` over that of `𝔪ᵢ ∩ A = 𝔪_A`; `ord` is `ordInt`. The source's
`dim A = 1` is `Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A`, which also admits the field case."]
theorem finite_maximalSpectrum_and_ordInt_norm_eq_finsum_inertiaDeg_mul_ordInt
    (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 A]
    [Algebra A B] [Module.Finite A B] (hAB : Function.Injective (algebraMap A B))
    (K L : Type*) [Field K] [Field L]
    [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K] [Algebra B L] [IsFractionRing B L]
    [Algebra K L] [Algebra A L] [IsScalarTower A K L] [IsScalarTower A B L] :
    Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) ∧
      ∀ (y : L) (hy : y ≠ 0),
        haveI : Module.Finite K L := finiteDimensional_fractionRing_of_finite A B K L hAB
        ordInt A (Algebra.norm K y) (Algebra.norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr hy) =
          ∑ᶠ v : MaximalSpectrum B, (v.asIdeal.inertiaDeg A : ℤ) *
            letI : Algebra (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
              IsLocalization.localizationAlgebraOfSubmonoidLe _ _ v.asIdeal.primeCompl
                (nonZeroDivisors B) v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
            haveI : IsScalarTower B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
              IsLocalization.localization_isScalarTower_of_submonoid_le _ _
                v.asIdeal.primeCompl (nonZeroDivisors B) v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
            haveI : IsFractionRing (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
              IsFractionRing.isFractionRing_of_isDomain_of_isLocalization v.asIdeal.primeCompl _ _
            haveI : IsNoetherianRing B := IsNoetherianRing.of_finite A B
            haveI := Ring.krullDimLE_one_localization_atPrime_of_finite A B v.asIdeal
            ordInt (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) y hy := by
  classical
  have : FaithfulSMul A B := (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective A B).mpr hAB
  have : Algebra.IsIntegral A B := Algebra.IsIntegral.of_finite A B
  have : Algebra.IsAlgebraic A B := Algebra.IsIntegral.isAlgebraic
  have hfin : Finite (MaximalSpectrum B) :=
    Stacks.OrderOfVanishing.DegreeInequality.finite_maximalSpectrum (A := A)
  refine ⟨hfin, fun y hy => ?_⟩
  have : Module.Finite K L := finiteDimensional_fractionRing_of_finite A B K L hAB
  have : IsNoetherianRing B := IsNoetherianRing.of_finite A B
  have : Fintype (MaximalSpectrum B) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  let algL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, Algebra (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L := fun v =>
    IsLocalization.localizationAlgebraOfSubmonoidLe _ _ v.asIdeal.primeCompl (nonZeroDivisors B)
      v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have towL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, IsScalarTower B (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
    fun v => IsLocalization.localization_isScalarTower_of_submonoid_le _ _
      v.asIdeal.primeCompl (nonZeroDivisors B) v.asIdeal.primeCompl_le_nonZeroDivisors
  have fracL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, IsFractionRing (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) L :=
    fun v => IsFractionRing.isFractionRing_of_isDomain_of_isLocalization v.asIdeal.primeCompl _ _
  have kdL : ∀ v : MaximalSpectrum B, Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (Localization.AtPrime v.asIdeal) :=
    fun v => Ring.krullDimLE_one_localization_atPrime_of_finite A B v.asIdeal
  rw [ord_norm_eq_sum_inertiaDeg_mul_ord A B K L hAB y hy _ rfl
    (Algebra.norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr hy), finsum_eq_sum_of_fintype]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun v _ => ?_
  have := v.isMaximal
  have : v.asIdeal.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) :=
    ⟨(IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal
      (Ideal.isMaximal_under_of_isIntegral_of_isMaximal (R := A) v.asIdeal)).symm⟩
  congr 2
  simp only [Ideal.inertiaDeg_eq_of_isMaximal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) v.asIdeal]
  simp

end
